{
  "rules": [
    "Horizon-dependent bias: model is slightly too high in the first ~1–12 days (typically +0.3 to +2 EUR), then becomes too low in the back half (~day 20–30), missing sustained rallies (often -1 to -10 EUR by the end).",
    "Trend underreaction / lag: when the market transitions into an uptrend, the model follows but with insufficient slope; it underestimates cumulative gains and peaks, especially after day ~18.",
    "Premature mean reversion: forecasts tend to revert toward mid/high-60s even when realized prices keep trending upward; reduce mean-reversion strength when recent momentum is positive.",
    "Spike/acceleration miss: during strong upside acceleration (late-horizon in examples), the model caps highs too early; apply an upside extension when last 5–10 days show rising highs and higher closes.",
    "Asymmetry: model handles drawdowns/soft patches better than upside breakouts; use a regime switch—if recent volatility + momentum are high and positive, shift the whole forward curve upward, increasingly with horizon."
  ]
}
